WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.101
The song that reminds me
of my family is,

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.503
"May the Circle Be Unbroken."

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.938
We used to sing that
on road trips.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.205
I don't even know
what that song is.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:07.506
We were a real church-family.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.142
BRIDGET EVERETT:
I'm not much of a church person.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.076
We went on holidays and...
when somebody died.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:13.413
So, if a lot of people die,
like in rapid succession, then,

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.548
I guess, I could call myself
a "church person."

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.684 line:0%
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:20.653
"Piece of My Heart"

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.022 line:0%
is a song that represents
freedom to me because

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.258
when I first moved
to New York, the only chance

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.459
I was getting to sing
was at karaoke bars.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.962
<i> And so I would sing
 "Piece of My Heart" and,</i>

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.964
rip my shirt and,
take shots and,

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.466
you know, spit 'em out
on the people,

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.035
and it was, uh, pretty magical,
at least for me.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.772
Oh, it was magical for everyone.
I know that for a fact.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.410
My song that is freedom is
"You Oughta Know"

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.678
by Alanis Morissette.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:46.712
That's my other karaoke song.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:47.646
-Is it really?
-Yes!

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:49.382
-That was my karaoke song.
-Oh, my god!

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.583
And, in fact,
it's my audition song

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.685
whenever you have to
do a "pop-rock" song

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:53.886
for musical theater.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:56.022
I'm so afraid of
expressing anger in life.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.457
You know, it's my own block.

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:03.929
You get to be so angry
in that song. You get to scream.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.631
-Feels good.
-Feels good to be angry.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:07.500
-We're all hurting.
-(JEFF HILLER LAUGHS)

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.568
We're all broken.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.470
It is like<i> The View.</i>

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:13.939
-Oh! That's him!
-Oh, god!

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:15.007
Get down!

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.510
I loved shooting in the car
because that was really when

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.045
-our characters, I felt like--
-Found each other.

00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:21.714
-Kinda found each other.
-Yeah, I agree.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:26.453
And it was also fun to have
sort of low-stakes stunts.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.458
-Is driving a stunt?
-It was for me.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.425
Don't hesitate.

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:35.528
BOTH: Don't hesitate.
Don't hesitate!

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.462
(TIRES SQUEALING)

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:37.830
I think
one of my favorite things

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:38.865
about this show is, like,

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.267
the sweet relationship between
Joel and Sam.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.702
And you know when you're, like,
finding a friend

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.370
and falling in love
with your friend...

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.906
Um, that's what
the car chase allows for,

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.342
so I think
it's really very tender.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.610
Right.

